{
  "id": "P1-W02-M1",
  "title": "One command = fork, exec, wait (and everything is inherited)",
  "alt": "A shell command box above the six things the shell does before your program starts. To the right, the parent process forks a child, an arrow trying to send an environment change back up is crossed out in red, and the child's three inherited file descriptors show only stdout redirected to a file. Below, the nine permission bits are drawn as a three-by-three grid mapping rwxr-x--- to octal 750, and the child's exit status 1 returns to the parent as dollar-question-mark.",
  "width": 1000,
  "height": 660,
  "tier": "T2",
  "week": 2,
  "elements": [
    {
      "type": "box",
      "id": "term",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 88,
      "w": 380,
      "h": 46,
      "label": "$ grep foo big.log > out.txt",
      "color": "ink",
      "size": 15
    },
    {
      "type": "arrow",
      "id": "adown",
      "x1": 230,
      "y1": 138,
      "x2": 230,
      "y2": 166,
      "color": "ink"
    },
    {
      "type": "box",
      "id": "shell",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 170,
      "w": 380,
      "h": 192,
      "color": "structure"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "shh",
      "x": 230,
      "y": 192,
      "text": "the shell, before anything runs",
      "size": 15,
      "bold": true,
      "color": "structure",
      "w": 360
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "st1",
      "x": 62,
      "y": 220,
      "text": "1.  expand globs, $VARS, quotes",
      "size": 14,
      "anchor": "start",
      "w": 360
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "st2",
      "x": 62,
      "y": 244,
      "text": "2.  resolve the name on $PATH",
      "size": 14,
      "anchor": "start",
      "w": 360
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "st3",
      "x": 62,
      "y": 268,
      "text": "3.  fork()   <- now there are two",
      "size": 14,
      "anchor": "start",
      "w": 360
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "st4",
      "x": 62,
      "y": 292,
      "text": "4.  redirect fds IN THE CHILD",
      "size": 14,
      "anchor": "start",
      "w": 360
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "st5",
      "x": 62,
      "y": 316,
      "text": "5.  exec()   <- grep replaces the copy",
      "size": 14,
      "anchor": "start",
      "w": 360
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "st6",
      "x": 62,
      "y": 340,
      "text": "6.  wait()   <- collect the exit code",
      "size": 14,
      "anchor": "start",
      "w": 360
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "n2",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 416,
      "w": 380,
      "text": "this is why cd is a builtin. A child cannot change its parent's directory, so an external cd would do nothing at all."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "m1",
      "x": 230,
      "y": 494,
      "text": "fork + exec  =  1.29 ms, measured",
      "size": 15,
      "w": 400
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "m2",
      "x": 230,
      "y": 528,
      "text": "10 000 loops: 0.013 s as a builtin vs 12.863 s calling an external command = 989x",
      "size": 13,
      "color": "muted",
      "w": 380
    },
